      "hints": [
        "Rearrange $y = 25 - 2(x+3)^2 \\implies (x+3)^2 = \\frac{25-y}{2}$.",
        "Take positive root: $g^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{25-x}{2}} - 3$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Set $y = 25 - 2(x + 3)^2$ and make $(x + 3)^2$ the subject:\n$$2(x + 3)^2 = 25 - y \\implies (x + 3)^2 = \\frac{25 - y}{2}$$",
        "Take the square root, choosing the positive root since $x \\ge -3$:\n$$x + 3 = \\sqrt{\\frac{25 - y}{2}} \\implies x = \\sqrt{\\frac{25 - y}{2}} - 3$$",
        "Express the inverse function in terms of $x$:\n$$g^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{25 - x}{2}} - 3$$"
